Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:54:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] win32u: List the virtual modes at the display's own
 frequency below 60Hz.

The virtual modes are every size at 60Hz and, when the display runs
faster, every size again at the display's own frequency. A display
that runs slower gets no entry at its own frequency, but the current
mode keeps it: EnumDisplaySettings(ENUM_CURRENT_SETTINGS) returns the
initial mode with the display's frequency until a mode is set.
find_display_mode skips every entry whose frequency differs from a
requested one above 1, so handing that DEVMODE back to
ChangeDisplaySettingsEx fails with DISP_CHANGE_BADMODE, and so does a
request that copies it and changes only the size, as games do. The Mac
driver reports the frequency in whole hertz, so this happens on any
display at 59Hz or below: a 59.94Hz monitor reads 59, and a 30Hz 4K
panel reads 30. The d3d9 tests that save and restore the display mode
fail on such a display with "Failed to restore display modes", and
later tests in the same process run on the mode that was left behind.

List every size at the display's own frequency below 60Hz as well, as
above it. 60Hz itself would only repeat the entries, and a frequency
of 0 or 1 is unknown, so those still add nothing. The modes are sorted
with the higher frequency first, so a request that names no frequency
still gets 60Hz on such a display.

A display in portrait orientation is still not covered: its initial
size is listed with width and height swapped, so its current mode
matches no entry at any frequency.

(cherry picked from commit d31cfb7706be2f8eb752fa1ac233f6e517915678)
---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index 83685fa5882..b2aa3b1ddb7 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -2245,7 +2245,7 @@ static DEVMODEW *get_virtual_modes( const DEVMODEW *initial, const DEVMODEW *max
         center_modes = !strcmp( env, "359870" );
 
     freqs[1] = devmode_get( initial, DM_DISPLAYFREQUENCY );
-    if (freqs[1] <= 60) freqs[1] = 0;
+    if (freqs[1] <= 1 || freqs[1] == 60) freqs[1] = 0;
 
     if (!(screen_sizes = get_screen_sizes( maximum, host_modes, host_modes_count, &sizes_count ))) return NULL;
     modes = malloc( (2 * ARRAY_SIZE(freqs) * ARRAY_SIZE(depths) * (sizes_count + 2) + 1) * sizeof(*modes) );
